<exercises xml:id="s_piecewise_absval_ex">
<exercise>
                <statement>

                <p>
                    Sketch the graph of the given function and evaluate it at
                    the given points.
                    
            <ol marker="(a)"><li>

                            <p>
                                <m>f(x)=</m>
                            </p>
                                        </li>

            <li>

                            <p>
                                <m>g(x)=</m>
                            </p>
                                        </li></ol>
                            </p>
</statement>
            </exercise>
<exercise>
                <statement>

                <p>
                    Find all the real values of <m>x</m> that satisfy the
                    following inequalities.
                    Write your answer using interval notation or set builder
                    notation.
                    <ol marker="(a)">
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\left| 2x+1\right|\leq 3</m>
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\left|3x-2\right|&gt;4</m>
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\left| 2x+1\right|\leq 0</m>
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\left| 2x+1\right|&lt; 0</m>
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\left| 2x+1\right|\geq 0</m>
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\left| 2x+1\right|&gt;0</m>
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </p>
                            </statement>
                    <solution>
                        <p>
<ol marker="(a)">
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        Note that you can use a sign chart to
                                        solve these exercises.
                                        <md>
                                            \left| 2x+1\right|\leq 3
                                        </md>
                                        <md>
                                            -3&lt;2x+1&lt;3
                                        </md>
                                        <md>
                                            -4&lt;2x&lt;2
                                        </md>
                                        <md>
                                            -2&lt;x&lt;1
                                        </md>
                                        Thus, the solution is the interval
                                        <m>(-2,1)</m>.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        <md>
                                            \left|3x-2\right|&gt;4
                                        </md>
                                        <md>
                                            3x-2&gt;4 \text{ or }3x-2&lt;-4
                                        </md>
                                        <md>
                                            3x&gt;6 \text{ or }3x&lt;-2
                                        </md>
                                        <md>
                                            x&gt;2 \text{ or }x&lt;-\dfrac{2}{3}
                                        </md>
                                        Thus, the solution is
                                        <m>(-\infty,-\dfrac{2}{3})\cup(2,\infty)</m>
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        Note that there are no <m>x</m> such
                                        that <m>|2x+1|&lt;0</m>, so we only need
                                        to solve the equation <m>|2x+1|=0</m>.
                                        <md>
                                            |2x+1|=0
                                        </md>
                                        <md>
                                            2x+1=0
                                        </md>
                                        <md>
                                            x=-\dfrac{1}{2}
                                        </md>
                                        Thus, the solution is the set
                                        <m>\{-\dfrac{1}{2}\}</m>
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        Since there are no such <m>x</m> such
                                        that <m>|2x+1|&lt;0</m>, the solution is
                                        <m>\emptyset</m>.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        Since <m>|2x+1|\geq0</m> for all
                                        <m>x</m>, the solution is
                                        <m>\mathbb{R}</m>.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        <m>|2x+1|&gt;0</m> for all <m>x</m>
                                        except when <m>|2x+1|=0</m>, i.e.,
                                        <m>x\in\mathbb{R}\setminus \{-1/2\}=(-\infty,-1/2)\cup(-1/2,\infty)</m>.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        </ol>
</p>
                    </solution>
            </exercise>
<exercise>
                <statement>

                <p>
                    Determine whether the following statements are true or
                    false.
                    Justify your reasoning.
                    <ol marker="(a)">
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>|a+b|=|a|+|b|</m> for all real numbers
                                <m>a,b</m>.
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>|ab|=|a||b|</m> for all real numbers
                                <m>a,b</m>.
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\left|\dfrac{a}{b}\right|=\dfrac{|a|}{|b|}</m>
                                for all real numbers <m>a,b</m>.
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                If <m>x</m> is a real number such that
                                <m>|x-2|&lt;3</m>, then <m>|3x-6|&lt;10</m>.
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                If <m>x</m> is a real number such that
                                <m>|3x-6|&lt;10</m>, then <m>|x-2|&lt;3</m>.
                                
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </p>
                            </statement>
                    <solution>
                        <p>
<ol marker="(a)">
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        False.
                                        For example, the equality is not true if
                                        <m>a=-1, b=1</m>.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        True.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        False.
                                        If <m>b=0</m>, neither side of the
                                        equality is defined.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        True.
                                        Multiply both sides of <m>|x-2|&lt;3</m>
                                        by <m>3</m> to get <m>3|x-2|&lt;9</m>,
                                        which is equivalent to
                                        <m>|3x-6|&lt;9</m>.
                                        But <m>9&lt;10</m>, so
                                        <m>|3x-6|&lt;10</m>
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        <li>
                                    <p>
                                        False.
                                        If we try to use the same idea as before
                                        and multiply by <m>1/3</m>, we get
                                        <m>|x-2|&lt;\dfrac{10}{3}</m>, but
                                        <m>\dfrac{10}{3}&gt;3</m>.
                                        Hence, any value of <m>x</m>, such that
                                        <m>3&lt;|x-2|&lt;10/3</m> will make this
                                        statement false.
                                        For example, if you take <m>x=5.2</m>,
                                        <m>|3\cdot 5.2-6|&lt;10</m>, but
                                        <m>|5.2-2|&gt;3</m>.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                        </ol>
</p>
                    </solution>
            </exercise>
